# #5851 O2c (a5e2e2ef, #5851 comment 6665050221): the split's cap hands the sibling the
# donor's committed read frontier, never more, when the hint guard fails.
MODULE: SiblingHintHonestSplitCapAboveFrontier
TARGET: SiblingHintHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the cap hands the sibling the heads as its hint, as D4 would, though the hint guard failed, so records between the donor's frontier and the heads are not in the rows
PERTURBS: SplitCap
BOUNDS: WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithSplitHint = TRUE, WithDuplicate = FALSE, WithViewOverlap = TRUE, WithSplitCap = TRUE

--- FIND
    /\ sibHint' = rp[a]
    /\ sibRows' = {o \in cache[a] : o <= rp[a]}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the cap reads the heads, not the committed frontier.
    /\ sibHint' = sh[a] - 1
    /\ sibRows' = {o \in cache[a] : o < sh[a]}
--- END
